# Market orders, time in force, and post-only orders.
> add ACME
added ACME
> sell 50 @ 101.00
ACME #1 SELL 50 @ 101.00 -> resting 50
> sell 50 @ 101.50
ACME #2 SELL 50 @ 101.50 -> resting 50

# A market order sweeps the book. Whatever it can't fill is cancelled rather than left resting.
> buy 120 market
ACME #3 BUY 120 @ market -> filled 100, cancelled the unfilled 20
  trade #1  50 @ 101.00  buy #3  sell #1
  trade #2  50 @ 101.50  buy #3  sell #2

# IOC trades what it can at its limit and cancels the rest.
> sell 50 @ 102.00
ACME #4 SELL 50 @ 102.00 -> resting 50
> buy 80 @ 102.00 ioc
ACME #5 BUY 80 @ 102.00 IOC -> filled 50, cancelled the unfilled 30
  trade #3  50 @ 102.00  buy #5  sell #4

# FOK is all or nothing: 40 is more than the 30 offered, so nothing trades. 30 fills in full.
> sell 30 @ 102.50
ACME #6 SELL 30 @ 102.50 -> resting 30
> buy 40 @ 102.50 fok
ACME #7 BUY 40 @ 102.50 FOK -> killed: there wasn't enough to fill all 40
> buy 30 @ 102.50 fok
ACME #8 BUY 30 @ 102.50 FOK -> filled 30
  trade #4  30 @ 102.50  buy #8  sell #6

# Post-only orders must add liquidity: one that would trade is rejected instead.
> sell 10 @ 103.00
ACME #9 SELL 10 @ 103.00 -> resting 10
> buy 10 @ 103.00 post-only
ACME #10 BUY 10 @ 103.00 post-only -> rejected: POST_ONLY_WOULD_CROSS
> buy 10 @ 102.75 post-only
ACME #11 BUY 10 @ 102.75 post-only -> resting 10

# DAY orders expire at the end of the day; GTC orders stay.
> sell 20 @ 104.00 day
ACME #12 SELL 20 @ 104.00 DAY -> resting 20
> expire
expired 1 day order: ACME #12
> book
ACME  CONTINUOUS  last 102.50  resting 2
              BID                       ASK
     102.75 x 10      (1)      103.00 x 10      (1)
